/// Diba as a Material 3 theme.
///
/// Two things about this brand fight Material's defaults, and both are handled
/// below rather than left for the app to rediscover.
///
/// First: do not rebuild this with ColorScheme.fromSeed(). That runs the seed
/// through Material's tonal algorithm and takes primary at tone 40, which
/// assumes primary is a colour that holds *white* text. Diba's primary is a
/// gold that holds dark text, so fromSeed returns a dark olive and the brand
/// disappears.
///
/// Second, and less obvious: Material spends ColorScheme.primary on two
/// different jobs. It fills things that carry a label — FilledButton, the FAB —
